From: postmarketOS mojito port
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath10k: qmi: register for the pin connect result indication

The downstream icnss driver registers for pin_connect_result in the WLFW indication register
request; ath10k does not. Candidate fix for SM6150 MPSS.AT.4.4 firmware rejecting the capability
request (QMI error 119) and asserting in wlan_process. UNTESTED on hardware.
---
diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath10k/qmi.c b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath10k/qmi.c
index 08a64f737..1b9144de3 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath10k/qmi.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath10k/qmi.c
@@ -763,6 +763,14 @@ ath10k_qmi_ind_register_send_sync_msg(struct ath10k_qmi *qmi)
 	req.fw_ready_enable = 1;
 	req.msa_ready_enable_valid = 1;
 	req.msa_ready_enable = 1;
+	/*
+	 * Register for the pin connect result like the downstream icnss driver
+	 * does. Some modem WLAN firmware (SM6150 MPSS.AT.4.4) waits for a client
+	 * of this indication before answering the capability request; without it
+	 * the request is rejected (QMI error 119) and wlan_process asserts.
+	 */
+	req.pin_connect_result_enable_valid = 1;
+	req.pin_connect_result_enable = 1;
 
 	if (ar_snoc->xo_cal_supported) {
 		req.xo_cal_enable_valid = 1;
